COMPI Turbulence Anisotropy Experiment
Timothy Sliwinski
CIRA / CSU / NOAA GSL

This experiment is the basis for the finite-differencing component of the COMPI 
project, where COMPI's goals are to COMPare Invariants between models with 
different numerical schemes for turbulent flows.

At the core of this experiment is a Taylor Green vortex configuration with 
varying grid anisotropy.


